    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, here, I think there's a dichotomy. When I said this to President Trump himself, I said, when you campaigned, I said to him, you campaigned as a populist against both the Democratic and Republican establishments. But you're governing as a hard right ideologue. You're capping it as hard right. Your ACA proposal, Trump care is hard right. Your proposal on taxes looks like it's hard right. So he would never have one campaigning on a hard-right platform because the hard-right is so far away from where the rest of America is. It's even far away from where the average Republican is. But since he doesn't really care about the issues, and I think Pence, who's a hard-right guy, Priebus, who just went along with the hard-right stuff, They sort of packed the cabinet and are directing the president in a hard right direction. And I think his presidency is going to be is not going to succeed at all because of that.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
