    "turn_text": "I think he does not at all. I don't think issues matter to him very much. But those two hard rights still tend. Well, I think the hard right that favors special interests, big business tax cuts on the wealthy is the one that's predominating. I don't think Bannon's opposed to those, but his stuff would be more like the immigration executive order and things like that. But I don't think they conflict with each other. I think they coexist with each other. Each side lets the other do their thing. The business leadership probably didn't like the executive order, but because they're so panting to cut their taxes and so-called regulation, which we call protections, they go along.",
