    "turn_text": "Well, I don't know if they can put the pieces together because this tax break idea just doesn't work. And one of the greatest, there are three weaknesses up. First, 82 cents on the dollar goes not to building roads or water or sewer or power or broadband, but to pay back the bonds, the bonds that are issued. Second, it creates tolls in places where they build things, the way they were never told before. But third, and this will be real trouble for Mitch McConnell, you can't do anything in any rural areas because there's not enough of a revenue stream to pay back the bonds. And so how's he going to bring a bill to the floor that'll hardly do anything in so many of the rural states that make up his coalition?",
