    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 94536,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94536.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 69,
    "turn_text": "Look, when you lose an election like we did, you can easily blame the other side. And certainly Comey and the Russian hacking hurt our side a lot. You have to look at the election and figure out what you did wrong because when you lose to somebody who is so unpopular like Trump, you got to say, what did we do wrong?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "After losing an election, one should critically examine their own performance.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Losing an election makes it easy to blame the opposing side.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The actions of James Comey and allegations of Russian hacking negatively impacted our campaign.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Trump was widely considered an unpopular candidate.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "A loss against an unpopular opponent indicates significant internal flaws in the losing party's strategy or appeal.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Blaming external factors undermines accountability and hinders meaningful improvement.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Self-reflection after defeat is essential for future electoral success.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes the Democratic Party has a responsibility to learn from past failures.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Public perception of Trump’s unpopularity is a shared and accepted truth among the audience.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Correction / Challenge"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 94536,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94536.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 71,
    "turn_text": "And my view is that we did not have a bold, strong, sharp-edged economic message. And we're going to correct that. We're in the process of doing it now. We've come up with a strong infrastructure program. Yesterday we announced a family leave. program and platform. And we're going to have by the early summer, we will have a complete economic program that Democrats from Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren to Joe Manchin and Mark Warner can be proud of.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "We did not have a bold, strong, sharp-edged economic message.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "We are going to correct the lack of a bold, strong, sharp-edged economic message.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "We have developed a strong infrastructure program.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "We are currently in the process of correcting the economic message.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "We announced a family leave program and platform yesterday.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "By early summer, we will have a complete economic program.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The completed economic program will be something that Democrats including Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren can be proud of.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The completed economic program will be something that Democrats including Joe Manchin and Mark Warner can be proud of.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "A bold, strong, sharp-edged economic message is necessary for political success.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Democratic Party unity is achievable despite ideological diversity among its members.",
